# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# cloudflare / opennext build artifacts — regenerated by every build,
# hundreds of MB, and never safe to commit
/.open-next/
/.wrangler/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# /dist/ WAS ignored here, and must not be any more.
#
# Under the old arrangement the site lived at the repo root and scripts/
# build.mjs copied it into dist/ for deployment, so dist/ was a build
# artefact and ignoring it was right.
#
# That is no longer true. The site IS dist/ now — wrangler.jsonc points
# Cloudflare at ./dist, and it is generated by build.py outside this repo.
# With this line in place, git silently ignored all 82 files of the
# actual website while happily committing the deletion of the old one.

# Working documents, not code. SETUP-GUIDE.md has held a secret key.
SETUP-GUIDE.md
LEGAL-BLANKS.md

# Never. Secrets go on the Worker with `npx wrangler secret put`.
.dev.vars
